The legal texts come from the Journal officiel de la République du Mali and the "Codes en vigueur" page, both
published by the Secrétariat général du Gouvernement (SGG):

  Journal officiel de la République du Mali, https://sgg-mali.ml/fr/journal-officiel/le-journal-officiel.html
  (issues 1997 to 2026, retrieved 2026-10-28 and 2026-11-27), one PDF per issue;
  "Codes en vigueur", https://sgg-mali.ml/fr/journal-officiel/les-codes-consolides.html (retrieved 2026-11-27).
  The Code du travail copy there is a consolidation by droit-afrique.com, published by the SGG; only the text of the
  law is reproduced.

Attribution: "Texte officiel : Journal officiel de la République du Mali, Secrétariat général du Gouvernement
(sgg-mali.ml)."

sgg-mali.ml states no licence. Mali is a member of the African Intellectual Property Organization (OAPI); the Bangui
Agreement (Annex VII, article 6) excludes official texts of a legislative, administrative or judicial nature from
copyright protection.

Changes made by Lexifina: each issue's text layer was split into its acts and converted to one Markdown file per
article, one paragraph per line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; headings were gathered into one plan file
per act; visas, signatures and annexes were kept in their own files; individual acts (appointments, authorisations,
approvals) were not taken; and the texts were arranged as git commits dated on their in-force day. The wording of the
law was not changed. The Government of Mali does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
